# Shell scripts must always be stored (and checked out) with LF line
# endings — a CRLF shebang line ("#!/bin/sh\r") fails to parse inside a
# Linux container ("/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter"). This matters
# specifically because this repo is developed on Windows, where Git's
# common core.autocrlf=true setting would otherwise convert these to
# CRLF on checkout, silently breaking any *.sh file the next time someone
# clones/checks out fresh — force LF regardless of local git config.
*.sh text eol=lf
